&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the finance partner to senior leaders across Technology, Aviation, Member Care, Growth, Public Affairs, Legal, and People—building trusted relationships and becoming a go-to thought partner for their business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build dynamic, detailed, and scalable financial models to support annual budgets, quarterly re-forecasts, and long-range planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage opex and capex budgets in partnership with the business, and own department monthly budget vs. actuals processes with succinct, actionable commentary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empower business leaders to actively own their P&amp;amp;Ls by building intuitive reporting, leading financial reviews, and translating numbers into decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and clearly communicate key risks and opportunities across your business areas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help drive cost savings and new growth initiatives by building detailed business cases to evaluate and support decision making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support creation of Investor Relations, Board of Director, and Management Financial Review materials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and champion improvements to our forecasting tools and processes, including opportunities to leverage AI and automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you&#39;ll measure success:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong relationships and regular ongoing dialogue with senior functional leaders across the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business leaders who feel equipped to own and manage their P&amp;amp;Ls—and who come to you proactively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accuracy and timeliness of financial forecasting and reporting across your business areas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meaningful contribution to reducing forecast and approval cycle times&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quality and clarity of materials prepared for senior leadership and the Board&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tangible improvements to forecasting processes and tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;re great at:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5-7+ years of progressive FP&amp;amp;A experience, ideally in a high-growth or publicly traded company, with a track record of owning forecasting and planning processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep hands-on expertise with FP&amp;amp;A systems—NSPB, Hyperion, Anaplan, OneStream, or similar EPM/CPM platforms; experience leading a system implementation or major upgrade is a strong plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical horsepower, meaning you love building models and are equally comfortable translating complex financial data into clear, executive-ready narratives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A systems thinker: you spot process inefficiencies and have the instincts—and the follow-through—to fix them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative partner: you know that the best finance teams make the whole organization smarter, and you build trust with non-finance stakeholders naturally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curious about and actively exploring how AI and automation can be applied to FP&amp;amp;A workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s degree in Finance, Accounting, Economics, or a related analytical discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
